        "payload": "tree d03974e765a7d08cc0135a140fcf55d2ef106ac4\nparent 05bc2f53ce0cb239c17dbdd6b261bd2db7d2a940\nauthor FlashW <flashwayne00@gmail.com> 1790624912 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790624912 -0300\n\nwallet: accept uppercase addresses without amount in sendall\n\nsendall remembers the recipients given without an amount as the strings\nthe user passed, and later finds their outputs by comparing against\nEncodeDestination of each output script, which is the canonical\nlowercase form for bech32. An address given in uppercase, which is\nvalid bech32 and accepted by the rest of the wallet, never matches. Its\noutput then keeps the placeholder amount of 0 and sendall fails with\n\"Specified output amount to bcrt1q... is below dust threshold.\"\n\nStore the decoded destinations of those addresses instead and compare\nthem with the destinations of the outputs, so the match no longer\ndepends on how the address was written.",
